-MECC combines profile-guided initial placement with joint HBM/CPU retention for single-GPU MoE inference. Its allocation and admission rules reduce repeated weight delivery, while scheduling overlaps the remaining read/copy work with ready expert computation. On one A100, MECC gives 1.77$\times$ decode speedup over streaming and 1.12$\times$ over the Fiddler-style adapter.
+MECC compiles initial residency and carries expert reuse through joint HBM/CPU retention. The plan specifies capacities and expert IDs; runtime requests drive promotion, demotion, and delivery. State reuse amortizes initial placement across requests. E1 gives 1.77$\times$ decode speedup over streaming on one A100.
 
